    <string name="config_configure_help">&lt;br /&gt;ℹ️️&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_configuration_help">On this page, configure
        Watch Kit Pro. You can change:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        the visual design of the &lt;i&gt;watch face&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        the &lt;i&gt;complications&lt;/i&gt; displayed on the watch face; and&lt;br /&gt;
        the &lt;i&gt;settings&lt;/i&gt; for how the watch face operates.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Swipe to go back.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        🃏️&lt;br /&gt;️</string>
    <string name="config_configure_settings_help">On this page, configure
        &lt;i&gt;settings&lt;/i&gt; for how the watch face operates. You can
        change:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        whether &lt;i&gt;unread notifications&lt;/i&gt; are indicated;&lt;br /&gt;
        the &lt;i&gt;typeface&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        the colors for &lt;i&gt;ambient day&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;ambient night&lt;/i&gt;
        display.&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_complications_help">A &lt;i&gt;complication&lt;/i&gt; on a
        watch face is a customisable display of information. Tap on a complication to
        choose what it shows.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        In addition, on this page, the display may be customised for:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;count&lt;/i&gt; (the number of complications);&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;position&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;size&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;scale&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;text color&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;ring&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;background&lt;/i&gt; material.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Your complication configuration is separate to the &lt;i&gt;watch face&lt;/i&gt;
        you choose. You may select a new watch face, but your complications will remain as
        you configured them.&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_watch_face_preset_help">The visual design of a
        &lt;i&gt;watch face&lt;/i&gt; consists of the following elements:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;colors&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;materials&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;hands&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        the &lt;i&gt;dial&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        On this page, configure these or view a &lt;i&gt;visual history&lt;/i&gt; of previous watch
        faces.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Your watch face is separate to the &lt;i&gt;complications&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;settings&lt;/i&gt; you
        choose. You may select a new watch face, but your complications will remain as you
        configured them.&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_colors_materials_help">On this page, configure the colorway of
        four &lt;i&gt;colors&lt;/i&gt; displayed in the watch face.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        The &lt;i&gt;fill color&lt;/i&gt; is the main color for elements of the watch face, such as
        &lt;i&gt;hands&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;pips&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        The &lt;i&gt;accent color&lt;/i&gt; is a complimentary color that adds
        variation.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        The &lt;i&gt;highlight color&lt;/i&gt; is an opposing color for
        elements to stand out.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        The &lt;i&gt;background color&lt;/i&gt; is the main color for the watch face
        background.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Each element of the watch face has a &lt;i&gt;material&lt;/i&gt;, which determines what it
        looks like. There are four materials:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;fill highlight&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;accent fill&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;accent highlight&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;base accent&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_material_help">On this page, configure one of the
        four &lt;i&gt;materials&lt;/i&gt; displayed in the watch face.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Each material has the following attributes:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        two &lt;i&gt;colors&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        one &lt;i&gt;gradient&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        one &lt;i&gt;texture&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Each element of the watch face has a material, which determines what it looks
        like. The elements which use this material are listed above.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Note that the colors are shared among all four materials, so changing them here will
        affect the watch face elsewhere.&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_hands_help">On this page, configure the:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;hour hand&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;minute hand&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;second hand&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Each hand has the following attributes:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        hand &lt;i&gt;shape&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;length&lt;/i&gt; and
        &lt;i&gt;thickness&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        hand &lt;i&gt;stalk&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        hand &lt;i&gt;material&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        cutout &lt;i&gt;shape&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;material&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        By default, the minute and second hands follow the style of the hour hand. To make them
        different, use the &lt;i&gt;override&lt;/i&gt; switches.&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_dial_help">On this page, configure the:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        pip area &lt;i&gt;margin&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        pip area &lt;i&gt;background material&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        digit &lt;i&gt;display&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        digit &lt;i&gt;size&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        digit &lt;i&gt;rotation&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        digit &lt;i&gt;format&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        digit &lt;i&gt;material&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        which &lt;i&gt;pips&lt;/i&gt; to display, from the following:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;quarter pips (at 12, 3, 6, 9)&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;hour pips (at 1+2, 4+5, 7+8, 10+11)&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;i&gt;minute pips&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        Each set of pips has the following attributes:&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        pip &lt;i&gt;shape&lt;/i&gt;;&lt;br /&gt;
        pip &lt;i&gt;size&lt;/i&gt;; and&lt;br /&gt;
        pip &lt;i&gt;material&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;br /&gt;
        &lt;br /&gt;
        By default, the hour and minute pips follow the style of the three-hour pips. To make them
        different, use the &lt;i&gt;override&lt;/i&gt; switches.&lt;br /&gt;</string>
    <string name="config_configure_typeface_help">On this page, configure the
        &lt;i&gt;typeface&lt;/i&gt; (or font) of all text on the watch face.&lt;br /&gt;</string>

